{%- comment -%}
  sections/ds-product-main.liquid — Disrupted Studio custom PDP

  Replaces Horizon's `product-information` section entirely. Renders the
  full hero (breadcrumb + 7:5 grid of gallery left, info column right)
  with everything brutalist-styled and editable per-product via standard
  product fields + metafields. NO quantity selector. NO theme blocks —
  this section owns all of its content.

  ---
  DATA SOURCES
  ---

  PRODUCT FIELDS (Shopify built-in, no setup needed):
    product.title              → big H1 title
    product.type               → eyebrow caps text (e.g. "Photoshop Plugin")
    product.price              → main price (mono)
    product.compare_at_price   → strikethrough + auto LAUNCH -X% tag
    product.description        → long description below the form
    product.media              → gallery main + thumbnails
    product.collections        → first non-trivial collection = breadcrumb

  PRODUCT METAFIELDS (namespace: "disrupted", optional, per-product):
    badge_text       (string)                   → orange badge text (e.g. "NEW · v1.0"); hidden if blank
    tagline          (string)                   → short paragraph under the title

  Sub-CTA (label + anchor) lives in SECTION SETTINGS now, set per
  template — plugin / font / graphics / bundle each ship with the
  right copy and anchor preconfigured. See section schema below +
  templates/product.*.json. Metafields `demo_url` and `sub_cta_label`
  have been removed; their definitions can be cleaned up in admin.
    plugin_specs     (Plugin specs metaobject)   → typed plugin spec rows:
                                                   compat, format, file_size, license, updates, support
    font_specs       (Font specs metaobject)     → typed font spec rows:
                                                   family, glyphs, formats, language, license
    graphics_specs   (Graphics specs metaobject) → typed graphics spec rows:
                                                   items, formats, resolution, license, updates
    specs            (list of Spec metaobjects)  → generic fallback for unusual product types.
                                                   Each Spec has `label` + `value` text fields.

  Spec rendering priority:
    plugin_specs → font_specs → graphics_specs → specs (list) → legacy keys.
  First non-empty set wins. Section hides if all are empty.

  DEPRECATED (still works if set, lowest priority):
    compat / format / file_size / license / updates / support — old flat
    metafield keys. Use plugin_specs metaobject instead going forward.

  All metafields are OPTIONAL. Rows without a value just don't render.
  See docs/changes.md for the metafield definition setup steps.

  ---
  NOTES
  ---
  - Form submits natively (page reload). Phase 5 polish can upgrade to
    Horizon's <product-form-component> for AJAX + cart-drawer integration.
  - Variant picker is a simple <select> for multi-variant products; hidden
    for single-variant. Selected variant's ID is what the form posts.
  - Thumb-swap uses ~15 lines of vanilla JS at the bottom, scoped to this
    section. Respects prefers-reduced-motion via CSS.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign cs = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1'

  comment
    Breadcrumb: prefer the product's first non-"all"/"frontpage" collection.
  endcomment
  assign crumb_collection = nil
  for c in product.collections
    if c.handle != 'all' and c.handle != 'frontpage'
      assign crumb_collection = c
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Eyebrow: product.type, fall back to crumb collection title.
  endcomment
  assign eyebrow_text = product.type
  if eyebrow_text == blank and crumb_collection
    assign eyebrow_text = crumb_collection.title
  endif

  comment
    Badge: fully merchant-editable via the disrupted.badge_text metafield.
    Type anything ("NEW · v1.0", "BESTSELLER", "LIMITED"), or leave blank
    to hide entirely. No tag-based logic — explicit content control.
  endcomment
  assign badge_text = product.metafields.disrupted.badge_text.value

  comment
    Sale calc.
  endcomment
  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign saved = product.compare_at_price | minus: product.price
    assign discount_percent = saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price | round
  endif

  comment
    Optional content metafields.
  endcomment
  assign tagline = product.metafields.disrupted.tagline.value

  comment
    Sub-CTA: label + URL are now SECTION SETTINGS set per template
    (see templates/product.plugin.json, product.font.json, etc.) so
    each product type has its own hardcoded copy + anchor target
    without per-product metafield setup.

      plugin   → "Watch the demo"             → #video
      font     → "See the specimen"           → #specimen
      graphics → "Browse the pack"            → #features
      bundle   → "View bundle contents"       → #includes

    Was previously driven by product metafields `demo_url` and
    `sub_cta_label`. Those metafield definitions can be deleted from
    Settings → Custom data → Products — no template still reads them.

    URL-scheme allowlist: only http(s):// absolutes and same-origin
    paths (starting with `/` or `#`) are honoured. Anything else
    (e.g. a stray `javascript:` URI from a careless theme-editor edit)
    is treated as blank so the sub-CTA hides entirely. Defence-in-depth.
  endcomment
  assign sub_cta_label = section.settings.sub_cta_label | default: 'Watch the demo'
  assign raw_demo_url = section.settings.sub_cta_url
  assign demo_url = ''
  if raw_demo_url != blank
    if raw_demo_url contains '://'
      if raw_demo_url contains 'http://' or raw_demo_url contains 'https://'
        assign demo_url = raw_demo_url
      endif
    else
      assign first_char = raw_demo_url | slice: 0, 1
      if first_char == '/' or first_char == '#'
        assign demo_url = raw_demo_url
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Specs — resolved in priority order:
    1. plugin_specs metaobject  (Compat/Format/File size/License/Updates/Support)
    2. font_specs metaobject    (Family/Glyphs/Formats/Language/License)
    3. graphics_specs metaobject (Items/Formats/Resolution/License/Updates)
    4. specs (list of generic Spec metaobjects, free label+value)
    5. legacy flat keys (backward compat)
  endcomment
  assign plugin_specs   = product.metafields.disrupted.plugin_specs.value
  assign font_specs     = product.metafields.disrupted.font_specs.value
  assign graphics_specs = product.metafields.disrupted.graphics_specs.value
  assign specs_list     = product.metafields.disrupted.specs.value

  assign legacy_spec_keys   = 'compat,format,file_size,license,updates,support' | split: ','
  assign legacy_spec_labels = 'Compat,Format,File size,License,Updates,Support' | split: ','

  assign has_specs = false
  if plugin_specs or font_specs or graphics_specs
    assign has_specs = true
  elsif specs_list and specs_list.size > 0
    assign has_specs = true
  else
    for key in legacy_spec_keys
      assign v = product.metafields.disrupted[key].value
      if v != blank
        assign has_specs = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

<section class="ds-pdp color-{{ cs }}">
  <div class="ds-pdp__inner">

    {%- comment -%} ----- BREADCRUMB ----- {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="ds-pdp__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="ds-pdp__crumb-link">Home</a>
      <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- if crumb_collection -%}
        <a href="{{ crumb_collection.url }}" class="ds-pdp__crumb-link">{{ crumb_collection.title }}</a>
        <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-current">{{ product.title }}</span>
    </nav>

    {%- comment -%} ----- HERO ----- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ds-pdp__hero">

      {%- comment -%} ----- GALLERY ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ds-pdp__gallery"
           {%- if section.settings.auto_advance_to_second and product.media.size > 1 %} data-auto-advance="1"{% endif -%}>
        <div class="ds-pdp__gallery-main">
          {%- if product.featured_media -%}
            {{
              product.featured_media.preview_image
              | image_url: width: 1600
              | image_tag:
                loading: 'eager',
                fetchpriority: 'high',
                widths: '600,900,1200,1600',
                sizes: '(min-width: 900px) 56vw, 100vw',
                alt: product.title,
                class: 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img',
                id: 'ds-pdp-main-img-' | append: section.id
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img placeholder-svg' }}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Inset prev/next arrows — overlay the hero image, only rendered
            when more than one media item exists.  Wired up by the existing
            gallery script at the bottom of this section; arrow click =
            cycle to the prev/next thumbnail with wrap-around at ends.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="ds-pdp__gallery-nav ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev"
              data-ds-gallery-prev
              aria-label="Previous image"
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="ds-pdp__gallery-nav ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next"
              data-ds-gallery-next
              aria-label="Next image"
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </button>

            {%- comment -%}
              Counter overlay — small mono-caps "1 / N" pill in the
              bottom-right of the main media. Editorial gallery convention
              (Aimé Leon Dore, Telfar, Apple). Helps visitors realize
              there's more media to scroll through.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="ds-pdp__gallery-counter" aria-hidden="true">
              <span data-counter-current>1</span>
              <span class="ds-pdp__gallery-counter-sep">/</span>
              <span data-counter-total>{%- assign max_render = 12 -%}{%- if product.media.size > max_render -%}{{ max_render }}{%- else -%}{{ product.media.size }}{%- endif -%}</span>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Pagination row — renders either thumbnail grid (utility
            ecommerce style) or dot row (editorial / luxury style)
            based on the gallery_pagination_style section setting.
            Both modes share the same data attributes so the JS
            (activate / step / swipe) is identical — only visuals
            change.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign pagination_style = section.settings.gallery_pagination_style | default: 'thumbnails' -%}
          {%- assign render_limit = 12 -%}
          {%- if pagination_style == 'thumbnails' -%}{%- assign render_limit = 8 -%}{%- endif -%}

          <div class="ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--{{ pagination_style }}">
            {%- for media in product.media limit: render_limit -%}
              {%- assign is_video = false -%}
              {%- assign video_src = '' -%}
              {%- if media.media_type == 'video' -%}
                {%- assign is_video = true -%}
                {%- for source in media.sources -%}
                  {%- if source.format == 'mp4' -%}
                    {%- assign video_src = source.url -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endif -%}

              <button
                type="button"
                class="ds-pdp__gallery-thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}{% if is_video %} ds-pdp__gallery-thumb--video{% endif %}"
                data-src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
                data-media-type="{% if is_video %}video{% else %}image{% endif %}"
                {%- if is_video %}
                  data-video-src="{{ video_src }}"
                  data-video-poster="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
                {%- endif %}
                aria-label="View {% if is_video %}video{% else %}image{% endif %} {{ forloop.index }}"
              >
                {%- comment -%}
                  Thumb preview image — only rendered in 'thumbnails'
                  mode. Dots are pure CSS circles with no image.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if pagination_style == 'thumbnails' -%}
                  {{
                    media.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 200
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      alt: '',
                      class: 'ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-img'
                  }}
                  {%- if is_video -%}
                    <span class="ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-play" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ----- INFO COLUMN ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ds-pdp__info">

        {%- comment -%}
          EYEBROW + OPTIONAL BADGE.  All four sources here are
          merchant-controlled text — Shopify Liquid doesn't auto-
          escape `{{ }}` output, so we explicitly | escape any
          metafield-driven text to be safe against a stray HTML/JS
          paste into the metafield value.  Defense in depth.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if eyebrow_text != blank or badge_text != blank -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-eyebrow">
            {%- if eyebrow_text != blank -%}
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-cat">{{ eyebrow_text | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if badge_text != blank -%}
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-badge">{{ badge_text | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} TITLE — product.title is sanitised by Shopify, no escape needed {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="ds-pdp__info-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>

        {%- comment -%}
          AGGREGATE STAR RATING. Auto-computed from any testimonials
          on the page that JS detects as linked to this product
          (i.e. cards with .ds-testimonials__item--current). Hidden by
          default; JS reveals + fills it after the testimonials section
          renders. Falls back to invisible (graceful degradation) if
          there are no linked testimonials or JS doesn't run.

          Placement: directly under the title, above the tagline. This
          is the slot Yotpo / Judge.me / Stamped / every review app
          uses by convention — visitors expect it here.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="ds-pdp__info-rating"
          data-ds-rating
          hidden
          aria-live="polite"
        >
          <span class="ds-pdp__info-rating-stars" data-ds-rating-stars aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="ds-pdp__info-rating-text" data-ds-rating-text></span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} TAGLINE (metafield) {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if tagline != blank -%}
          <p class="ds-pdp__info-tagline">{{ tagline | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          PRICE ROW (price + compare-at + sale tag inline)

          All three spans always render so the JS variant-change handler
          can update them in place without re-parsing markup. The strike
          + discount spans use `hidden` when the current variant has no
          compare-at price; JS toggles the attribute on switch.

          on_sale + discount_percent are recalculated from the CURRENT
          variant's compare-at (was previously product.compare_at_price,
          which doesn't reflect per-variant pricing — e.g., a free
          Personal variant + a paid Commercial variant where only one
          is "on sale" relative to its own compare-at).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign cv_on_sale = false
          assign cv_discount_pct = 0
          if current_variant.compare_at_price and current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price
            assign cv_on_sale = true
            assign cv_saved = current_variant.compare_at_price | minus: current_variant.price
            assign cv_discount_pct = cv_saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: current_variant.compare_at_price | round
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="ds-pdp__info-price-row">
          <span class="ds-pdp__info-price" data-ds-price>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
          <span
            class="ds-pdp__info-price-strike"
            data-ds-compare
            {% unless cv_on_sale %}hidden{% endunless %}
          >{%- if cv_on_sale -%}{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}{%- endif -%}</span>
          <span
            class="ds-pdp__info-sale-tag"
            data-ds-discount
            {% unless cv_on_sale %}hidden{% endunless %}
          >{%- if cv_on_sale -%}Launch −{{ cv_discount_pct }}%{%- endif -%}</span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          BUY FORM (ATC, no quantity)

          Wrapped in Horizon's <product-form-component> so the submit is
          intercepted, posted to /cart/add.js via AJAX, and a CartAddEvent
          is dispatched. The cart-drawer-component listens for that event
          and (because it has `auto-open`) slides itself open with the new
          item already inside — no full page reload.

          Required wiring:
            data-section-id          — for cart morphing
            data-product-id          — for analytics + variant events
            on:submit="/handleSubmit" — declarative intercept
            ref="liveRegion"         — SR announcement target (required)
            ref="variantId"          — current variant input (required)

          Variant products: the user-facing <select> drives a hidden
          <input name="id" ref="variantId"> that the component reads. A
          tiny inline listener keeps the two in sync on change.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script src="{{ 'product-form.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>

        <product-form-component
          data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
          data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
          on:submit="/handleSubmit"
          class="ds-pdp__info-form-component"
          data-skeleton-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
          data-skeleton-image="{%- if product.featured_image -%}{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 192 }}{%- endif -%}"
        >
          <div
            class="visually-hidden"
            aria-live="assertive"
            role="status"
            aria-atomic="true"
            ref="liveRegion"
          ></div>

          {%- form 'product', product, class: 'ds-pdp__info-form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Hidden input is always the one product-form-component reads.
              For variant products the visible <select> writes into it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input
              type="hidden"
              name="id"
              ref="variantId"
              value="{{ current_variant.id }}"
              data-ds-variant-input
            >
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">

            {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Tier-aware variant picker. If ANY variant has the
                `disrupted.tier_name` metafield set (Phase 2 license
                tier rollout), the picker renders as a stack of
                brutalist button cards — one per tier — with the tier
                name, summary, and price upfront. Otherwise (non-tier
                products like future color/size variants) falls back
                to the standard <select>.

                Both controls write into the same hidden
                [data-ds-variant-input] used by the AJAX add-to-cart
                form. The per-section sync script below handles either
                control type.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                # Tier-card mode kicks in in two ways:
                #   1. Strong signal: any variant has the disrupted.tier_name
                #      metafield set (Path B — richer labels with /seat info)
                #   2. Loose signal: the option name itself reads as
                #      "license"-ish or "tier"-ish (Path A — variants alone,
                #      no metafield setup required)
                # Either trigger renders the brutalist cards; merchant
                # picks whichever setup fits their workflow.
                assign use_tier_cards = false
                for v in product.variants
                  if v.metafields.disrupted.tier_name.value != blank
                    assign use_tier_cards = true
                    break
                  endif
                endfor
                unless use_tier_cards
                  assign opt_name_lc = product.options.first | default: '' | downcase
                  if opt_name_lc contains 'license' or opt_name_lc contains 'tier'
                    assign use_tier_cards = true
                  endif
                endunless
              -%}
              <div class="ds-pdp__info-variant">
                <div class="ds-pdp__info-variant-head">
                  <span class="ds-pdp__info-variant-label">
                    {{ product.options.first | default: 'Variant' }}
                  </span>
                  {%- if use_tier_cards -%}
                    <a
                      href="/pages/license"
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener"
                      class="ds-pdp__info-variant-link ds-text-link"
                    >
                      Compare tiers
                      <span class="ds-text-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                {%- if use_tier_cards -%}
                  <div
                    class="ds-pdp__tier-cards"
                    data-ds-variant-radio-group
                    role="radiogroup"
                    aria-label="License tier"
                  >
                    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                      {%- assign v_tier_name    = variant.metafields.disrupted.tier_name.value -%}
                      {%- assign v_tier_summary = variant.metafields.disrupted.tier_summary.value -%}
                      <label class="ds-pdp__tier-card">
                        <input
                          type="radio"
                          class="ds-pdp__tier-card-input"
                          name="ds-tier-{{ section.id }}"
                          value="{{ variant.id }}"
                          data-price="{{ variant.price }}"
                          data-compare-at="{{ variant.compare_at_price | default: 0 }}"
                          data-price-formatted="{{ variant.price | money | escape }}"
                          data-compare-formatted="{% if variant.compare_at_price and variant.compare_at_price > 0 %}{{ variant.compare_at_price | money | escape }}{% endif %}"
                          {% if variant.id == current_variant.id %}checked{% endif %}
                          {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                        >
                        <div class="ds-pdp__tier-card-content">
                          <div class="ds-pdp__tier-card-head">
                            <span class="ds-pdp__tier-card-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="ds-pdp__tier-card-name">{{ v_tier_name | default: variant.title }}</span>
                            <span class="ds-pdp__tier-card-price">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
                          </div>
                          {%- if v_tier_summary != blank -%}
                            <p class="ds-pdp__tier-card-summary">{{ v_tier_summary }}</p>
                          {%- endif -%}
                          {%- unless variant.available -%}
                            <p class="ds-pdp__tier-card-soldout">Sold out</p>
                          {%- endunless -%}
                        </div>
                      </label>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
                {%- else -%}
                  <select
                    id="ds-variant-{{ section.id }}"
                    class="ds-pdp__info-variant-select"
                    data-ds-variant-select
                  >
                    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                      <option
                        value="{{ variant.id }}"
                        data-price="{{ variant.price }}"
                        data-compare-at="{{ variant.compare_at_price | default: 0 }}"
                        data-price-formatted="{{ variant.price | money | escape }}"
                        data-compare-formatted="{{ variant.compare_at_price | money | escape }}"
                        {% if variant.id == current_variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                        {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                      >
                        {{ variant.title }} — {{ variant.price | money }}{% unless variant.available %} (sold out){% endunless %}
                      </option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endunless -%}

            <button
              type="submit"
              name="add"
              class="ds-btn ds-btn--lg ds-btn--full ds-pdp__info-cta"
              data-ds-main-atc
              {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
            >
              {%- if current_variant.available -%}
                Add to cart — <span data-ds-main-atc-price>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
              {%- else -%}
                Sold out
              {%- endif -%}
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
        </product-form-component>

        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Tiny per-section script: keep the hidden variantId input in
            sync with the user-facing variant picker so AJAX submits
            the right id. Handles both control types:
              • <select data-ds-variant-select>  (non-tier products)
              • [data-ds-variant-radio-group]    (tier mode — button cards)
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <script>
            (function () {
              var sec = document.getElementById('shopify-section-{{ section.id }}');
              if (!sec) return;
              var hidden = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-input]');
              if (!hidden) return;
              var atcPrice  = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-main-atc-price]');
              var priceEl   = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-price]');
              var compareEl = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-compare]');
              var discountEl = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-discount]');

              /* Read variant data off the control that just changed
                 (radio input or <option>) and update every price surface
                 the PDP exposes — main display price, strikethrough,
                 launch %, AND the ATC button price. Switching tiers now
                 updates ALL of them, not just the ATC button. */
              function applyVariant(control) {
                if (!control) return;
                var priceCents       = parseInt(control.getAttribute('data-price'), 10);
                var compareCents     = parseInt(control.getAttribute('data-compare-at'), 10) || 0;
                var priceFormatted   = control.getAttribute('data-price-formatted') || '';
                var compareFormatted = control.getAttribute('data-compare-formatted') || '';

                if (priceEl && priceFormatted) priceEl.textContent = priceFormatted;
                if (atcPrice && priceFormatted) atcPrice.textContent = priceFormatted;

                var onSale = compareCents > priceCents && compareCents > 0;
                if (onSale) {
                  if (compareEl) {
                    compareEl.textContent = compareFormatted;
                    compareEl.removeAttribute('hidden');
                  }
                  if (discountEl) {
                    var pct = Math.round((compareCents - priceCents) / compareCents * 100);
                    discountEl.textContent = 'Launch −' + pct + '%';
                    discountEl.removeAttribute('hidden');
                  }
                } else {
                  if (compareEl)  compareEl.setAttribute('hidden', '');
                  if (discountEl) discountEl.setAttribute('hidden', '');
                }
              }

              var select = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-select]');
              if (select) {
                select.addEventListener('change', function () {
                  hidden.value = select.value;
                  applyVariant(select.options[select.selectedIndex]);
                });
                return;
              }

              var radios = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-radio-group]');
              if (radios) {
                radios.addEventListener('change', function (e) {
                  if (!e.target || !e.target.matches('input[type="radio"]')) return;
                  hidden.value = e.target.value;
                  applyVariant(e.target);
                });
              }
            })();
          </script>
        {%- endunless -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          SUB-CTA (metafield demo_url).  `demo_url` was scheme-allowlisted
          above (http/https/`/`/`#` only); | escape on the href as a
          belt-and-braces attribute escape.  Same for sub_cta_label.

          The sub-CTA points to in-page anchors like #video, #features,
          #specimen, #includes. If the merchant's template doesn't
          include the matching section/block (e.g. plugin product
          page set up without a video block), the link would scroll
          to nothing. The wrapper is rendered with `hidden` and a
          data-target-id attribute; the small inline JS below
          un-hides it ONLY if the target element actually exists in
          the DOM. External http(s) URLs are always shown (they go
          off-site, no need to verify).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if demo_url != blank -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign sub_cta_first = demo_url | slice: 0, 1
            assign sub_cta_is_anchor = false
            if sub_cta_first == '#'
              assign sub_cta_is_anchor = true
              assign sub_cta_target_id = demo_url | remove_first: '#'
            endif
          -%}
          <div
            class="ds-pdp__info-sub-cta"
            {% if sub_cta_is_anchor %}
              data-ds-sub-cta-target="{{ sub_cta_target_id | escape }}"
              hidden
            {% endif %}
          >
            <a href="{{ demo_url | escape }}" class="ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-link">
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-text">{{ sub_cta_label | escape }}</span>
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          {%- if sub_cta_is_anchor -%}
            <script>
              (function () {
                var wrapper = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
                if (!wrapper || wrapper.dataset.dsSubCtaTarget == null) return;
                var targetId = wrapper.dataset.dsSubCtaTarget;
                if (!targetId) return;
                // Probe the DOM both now (in case the target has
                // already rendered) and on DOMContentLoaded (for
                // sections that render after this one).
                function probe() {
                  if (document.getElementById(targetId)) {
                    wrapper.removeAttribute('hidden');
                  }
                }
                probe();
                if (wrapper.hasAttribute('hidden')) {
                  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', probe);
                }
              })();
            </script>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} SPECS TABLE — typed sets (plugin/font/graphics) preferred, then generic, then legacy {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_specs -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-specs">
            {%- if plugin_specs -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.compat.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Compat</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.compat.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.format.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Format</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.format.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.file_size.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">File size</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.file_size.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.license.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value"><a href="/pages/license" class="ds-pdp__info-spec-link">{{ plugin_specs.license.value | escape }}</a></span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.updates.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Updates</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.updates.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.support.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Support</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.support.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif font_specs -%}
              {%- if font_specs.family.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Family</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.family.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.glyphs.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Glyphs</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.glyphs.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.formats.value  != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Formats</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.formats.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.language.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Language</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.language.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.license.value  != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value"><a href="/pages/license" class="ds-pdp__info-spec-link">{{ font_specs.license.value | escape }}</a></span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif graphics_specs -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.items.value      != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Items</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.items.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.formats.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Formats</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.formats.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.resolution.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Resolution</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.resolution.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.license.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value"><a href="/pages/license" class="ds-pdp__info-spec-link">{{ graphics_specs.license.value | escape }}</a></span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.updates.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Updates</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.updates.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif specs_list and specs_list.size > 0 -%}
              {%- for spec in specs_list -%}
                {%- assign label = spec.label.value -%}
                {%- assign value = spec.value.value -%}
                {%- if label != blank and value != blank -%}
                  <div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">{{ label | escape }}</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ value | escape }}</span></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- for key in legacy_spec_keys -%}
                {%- assign value = product.metafields.disrupted[key].value -%}
                {%- if value != blank -%}
                  <div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">{{ legacy_spec_labels[forloop.index0] }}</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ value | escape }}</span></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          LONG DESCRIPTION.

          Clamped to a few lines by default with a "Read more" toggle
          appended underneath. Clamp height is controlled by a CSS
          custom property so it's easy to tune. The button auto-hides
          on load if the description is short enough not to need it
          — see JS at bottom of the section.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.description != blank -%}
          <div
            class="ds-pdp__info-description-wrap"
            data-ds-desc
            data-clamp-lines="{{ section.settings.description_clamp_lines | default: 4 }}"
          >
            <div class="ds-pdp__info-description" data-ds-desc-body>
              {{ product.description }}
            </div>
            {%- comment -%}
              Toggle button. Starts hidden via attribute; JS reveals it
              only if the description actually overflows the clamp. No
              JS = no toggle = full description shown, which is the
              correct graceful degradation.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="ds-pdp__info-description-toggle"
              data-ds-desc-toggle
              aria-expanded="false"
              hidden
            >
              <span data-ds-desc-toggle-label-more>Read more</span>
              <span data-ds-desc-toggle-label-less hidden>Read less</span>
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-description-toggle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  ----- STICKY ADD-TO-CART BAR -----
  Appears at the top of the viewport once the user has scrolled past
  the main buybox, so the conversion path is always visible while
  reading features, FAQs, video, etc.

  Anatomy
    [ thumb 48px ] [ name + price ] [ + ADD TO CART ]

  Implementation
    • Lives OUTSIDE the main <section> so it's a sibling element with
      simple position:fixed positioning relative to viewport.
    • Hidden by default. JS adds `.is-visible` when the main ATC's
      bottom edge has scrolled above the header.
    • Wrapped in <product-form-component> so submitting it triggers
      AJAX add + opens the cart drawer (same flow as the main ATC).
    • Variant + price stay in sync with the main form via small JS
      bridge (listens for change on the variant select).
{%- endcomment -%}
<product-form-component
  class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta"
  data-ds-sticky-cta
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  on:submit="/handleSubmit"
  aria-hidden="true"
  data-skeleton-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
  data-skeleton-image="{%- if product.featured_image -%}{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 192 }}{%- endif -%}"
>
  <div class="visually-hidden" aria-live="assertive" role="status" aria-atomic="true" ref="liveRegion"></div>
  <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner">

    {%- comment -%} thumb (links to top of page) {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="#" class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media" aria-label="Back to top" data-ds-sticky-top>
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        {{
          product.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 120
          | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              alt: product.title,
              widths: '48,96,144',
              sizes: '48px',
              class: 'ds-pdp-sticky-cta__img'
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    {%- comment -%} name + price stack {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__info">
      <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name">{{ product.title }}</div>
      <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price">
        <span
          class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price-strike"
          data-ds-sticky-compare
          {% unless cv_on_sale %}hidden{% endunless %}
        >{%- if cv_on_sale -%}{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}{%- endif -%}</span>
        <span data-ds-sticky-price>{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ATC form — own product-form-component instance {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- form 'product', product, novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="id"
        ref="variantId"
        value="{{ current_variant.id }}"
        data-ds-sticky-variant
      >
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      <button
        type="submit"
        name="add"
        class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn"
        {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
      >
        {%- if current_variant.available -%}
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label">Add</span>
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long">Add to cart</span>
        {%- else -%}
          Sold out
        {%- endif -%}
      </button>
    {%- endform -%}
  </div>
</product-form-component>

{% style %}
  /* ds-pdp — port of mockup .pdp-* (lines 1528-1660) with ds- namespace */

  .ds-pdp {
    background: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
  .ds-pdp__inner {
    padding-left: var(--pad-x);
    padding-right: var(--pad-x);
  }

  /* Breadcrumb */
  .ds-pdp__crumb {
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-link {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-link:hover { color: var(--color-fg); }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-sep { opacity: 0.4; }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-current { color: var(--color-fg); }

  /* Hero grid: balanced columns. Gallery + info each get an equal
     half. Was 7fr / 5fr which made the gallery dominate the screen
     on wide desktops — pushed the buy box into a cramped corner
     and the gallery image read as oversized. */
  .ds-pdp__hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-9);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ds-pdp__hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }
  }

  /* Gallery — sticky on desktop so the image stays in view while
     the right column scrolls. Reverses the previous setup where
     info was sticky and gallery scrolled — that pattern lets long
     descriptions push the image off-screen, which is the worst
     possible thing on a software/visual product like Pixel Perfect.

     max-width caps the image at a sensible size on ultra-wide
     screens (otherwise 1fr 1fr at 1900px = 900px-wide gallery,
     way too dominant). */
  .ds-pdp__gallery {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 560px;
    width: 100%;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height, 64px) + var(--space-4));
    align-self: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery {
      max-width: 100%;
      position: static;
    }
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  /* Belt-and-suspenders: even without the `controls` attribute, iOS
     Safari sometimes paints a big "tap to play" disc on top of the
     video before it autoplays. These selectors suppress that overlay
     plus any native controls Chrome/Firefox might leak in. */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-video::-webkit-media-controls,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-video::-webkit-media-controls-start-playback-button,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-video::-webkit-media-controls-overlay-play-button {
    display: none !important;
    -webkit-appearance: none !important;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-video::-internal-media-controls-overlay-cast-button {
    display: none !important;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main .placeholder-svg {
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: var(--space-7);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     GALLERY NAV ARROWS
     Small prev/next buttons overlaid on the hero image.  Only
     render when product.media.size > 1.  Sit inside the existing
     `.ds-pdp__gallery-main` (position: relative), so the absolute
     positioning is local to the square image frame.
     Brutalist treatment: sharp corners, mono glyph, semi-opaque
     dark background, hover lifts opacity + accent border.
     ============================================================ */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    padding: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    border-radius: 0;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    z-index: 2;
    opacity: 0.65;
    transition:
      opacity var(--t-fast) var(--ease),
      background var(--t-fast) var(--ease),
      border-color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main:hover .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav:hover,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav:focus-visible {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    opacity: 1;
    outline: none;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev { left: 12px; }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next { right: 12px; }

  /* Touch devices: arrows always at full opacity (no hover state to reveal them). */
  @media (hover: none) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav { opacity: 0.85; }
  }

  /* Mobile: slightly smaller + tighter inset so they don't crowd the image. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
      width: 32px;
      height: 32px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev { left: 8px; }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next { right: 8px; }
  }

  /* Counter pill — bottom-right of the main media. Editorial gallery
     convention. Mono caps, dark translucent bg so it reads against
     any image. Hidden when product has ≤1 media (no overlay rendered). */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-counter {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 12px;
    right: 12px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 2;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-counter-sep {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  /* Base: thumbnail grid (default mode, used by font / graphics / bundle
     product templates where the merchant wants to show each media at a
     glance). */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--thumbnails {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--thumbnails .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    overflow: hidden;
    cursor: pointer;
    position: relative;
    transition: border-color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--thumbnails .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb:hover,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--thumbnails .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb.is-active {
    border-color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  /* Dot pagination — editorial mode. Small horizontal row of muted
     pills (rectangle for brutalist edge, not perfect circles), active
     pill fills with accent. Used on plugin templates where the
     demo video carries the whole story and a thumb grid would
     visually crowd it. */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 18px 0 4px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb {
    width: 18px;
    height: 4px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: var(--color-border-strong, var(--color-border));
    padding: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background var(--t-fast) var(--ease),
      width var(--t-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb:hover {
    background: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb.is-active {
    background: var(--color-fg);
    width: 32px;
  }
  /* Larger tap target on mobile — visible size stays small but the
     hit area grows via a transparent ::before that sits on top. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots {
      padding: 14px 0 2px;
    }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb {
      position: relative;
    }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs--dots .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: -12px -3px;
    }
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  /* Play-icon overlay on video thumbnails — signals "this is a video,
     clicking will load the player." White triangle inside a dark
     translucent disc, centered. Pure CSS, no SVG dependency. */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-play {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1;
    border-radius: 999px;
    pointer-events: none;
    text-indent: 2px; /* nudge glyph right of optical center */
  }

  /* Info column — scrolls naturally now (was sticky). The gallery
     is sticky instead, so the image stays in view as the visitor
     reads through the buy box → specs → description. When they
     reach the bottom of the info column, the gallery releases and
     the whole page scrolls to the next section. */
  .ds-pdp__info {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    /* Cap width on ultra-wide screens so the buy-box text doesn't
       balloon into a 900px-wide reading line — keeps everything
       proportional next to the 560px-capped gallery. */
    max-width: 560px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* Eyebrow + NEW badge row */
  .ds-pdp__info-eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-cat {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    /* Brutalist outlined chip — thin grey border, no fill, sharp corners */
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 0;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 7px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent-fg);
  }

  /* Title */
  .ds-pdp__info-title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 0.9;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Aggregate star rating — small horizontal row under the title. */
  .ds-pdp__info-rating {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
    /* Negative top margin pulls it closer to the title without a
       custom gap on the parent flex column (which would affect the
       title→tagline distance too). */
    margin-top: calc(var(--space-2) * -1);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-rating-stars {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-rating-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }

  /* Tagline */
  .ds-pdp__info-tagline {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Price row */
  .ds-pdp__info-price-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-price {
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-price-strike {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sale-tag {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-sale);
    padding: 3px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-sale);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  /* Form */
  .ds-pdp__info-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-micro);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-select {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    color: var(--color-fg);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    border-radius: 0;
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    /* Caret arrow */
    background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, currentColor 50%),
                      linear-gradient(135deg, currentColor 50%, transparent 50%);
    background-position: calc(100% - 20px) 50%, calc(100% - 14px) 50%;
    background-size: 6px 6px, 6px 6px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    padding-right: 36px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-select:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  /* Label row: variant label on the left, optional auxiliary link on
     the right (e.g. "Compare tiers →" when the picker is in tier-card
     mode). Mirrors the "View demo →" pattern used elsewhere on PDPs —
     keeps the secondary action paired with the section heading instead
     of orphaned below the control. */
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-link {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    /* Drop the border-bottom that .ds-text-link applies by default —
       this link sits paired with the variant label, not in a section
       footer, so the underline reads too heavy in context. */
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  /* On narrow viewports the link wraps under the label rather than
     squeezing into the same row — keeps it readable on phones. */
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .ds-pdp__info-variant-head {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
  }

  /* ----- Tier button cards (replaces <select> in tier mode) -----
     One card per variant, stacked. Each card is a <label> wrapping a
     visually-hidden radio input + visible content. The radio drives
     state via native form semantics; arrow keys, Space, and tab order
     work without any custom JS. Selection styling uses :has() and the
     adjacent-sibling combinator so it stays in sync with the radio. */
  .ds-pdp__tier-cards {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card:has(.ds-pdp__tier-card-input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: rgba(255, 77, 31, 0.05);
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card:has(.ds-pdp__tier-card-input:disabled) {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  /* Visually hide the native radio but keep it in the accessibility
     tree so keyboard + SR users get full control. */
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-input {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-input:focus-visible + .ds-pdp__tier-card-content {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* Custom radio dot — circular border, fills with accent on check. */
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-radio {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-background);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    position: relative;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card:has(.ds-pdp__tier-card-input:checked) .ds-pdp__tier-card-radio {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card:has(.ds-pdp__tier-card-input:checked) .ds-pdp__tier-card-radio::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 3px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-name {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-price {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  /* Summary line indents past the radio so it reads under the tier name,
     not under the radio dot. 14px radio + 12px gap = 26px indent. */
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-summary {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding-left: 26px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .ds-pdp__tier-card-soldout {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding-left: 26px;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .ds-pdp__info-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-cta:disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  /* Sub-CTA — full-width row with text left and arrow right, slot
     into the visual rhythm between the ATC button and the specs
     table. Bottom border doubles as a divider above the specs box
     below, so the whole right column reads as a continuous stack
     of tabular info rows instead of floating elements. */
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    width: 100%;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-fg);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: color var(--t-fast) var(--ease), border-color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-link:hover .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta-arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  /* Specs */
  .ds-pdp__info-specs {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-label {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-value {
    color: var(--color-fg);
    text-align: right;
  }
  /* License value links to /pages/license — inherit color, brutalist
     underline so it's obviously clickable without breaking the spec row
     visual rhythm. */
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-link {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* Long description — clamped wrapper.
     The wrapper holds margin so it doesn't jump when clamp toggles. */
  .ds-pdp__info-description-wrap {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  /* Body — line-clamps via -webkit-box. The clamp count is set
     dynamically on the wrapper via JS reading data-clamp-lines. */
  .ds-pdp__info-description {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    /* Clamp lives on the BODY (so the toggle button sits below the
       clipped content, not inside it). is-expanded removes it. */
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    -webkit-line-clamp: var(--ds-desc-clamp, 4);
    line-clamp: var(--ds-desc-clamp, 4);
    overflow: hidden;
    /* Fade the last visible line so the truncation reads as
       intentional rather than abruptly cropped. */
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 70%, transparent);
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 70%, transparent);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description-wrap.is-expanded .ds-pdp__info-description {
    -webkit-line-clamp: unset;
    line-clamp: unset;
    overflow: visible;
    mask-image: none;
    -webkit-mask-image: none;
  }
  /* Toggle button — minimal, mono caps, accent on hover. Sits below
     the clipped body with a small top margin. Hidden by default
     (rendered with [hidden] in Liquid); JS reveals it only when the
     body actually overflows. */
  .ds-pdp__info-description-toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding: 4px 0;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    text-decoration: underline;
    transition: color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .ds-pdp__info-description-toggle:hover {
      color: var(--color-accent);
    }
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description-toggle-arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform var(--t-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description-wrap.is-expanded .ds-pdp__info-description-toggle-arrow {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  .ds-pdp__info-description p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .ds-pdp__info-description strong { color: var(--color-fg); font-weight: 500; }
  .ds-pdp__info-description ul,
  .ds-pdp__info-description ol {
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
    /* Defensive override: kill any multi-column / grid styling the
       description HTML might bring in. Shopify's rich text editor
       has a "columns" feature, and pasted HTML from other sites
       sometimes carries inline `column-count` or `display: grid`
       on <ul>/<ol> — which renders bullets in too-narrow columns
       (2-word lines) instead of a flat readable list. !important
       because the offending styles can be INLINE on the element. */
    column-count: 1 !important;
    columns: auto !important;
    display: block !important;
    grid-template-columns: none !important;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    /* Items in a CSS column or grid can carry inline width — reset */
    break-inside: auto;
  }

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------
     Mobile (≤600px) — phone-specific tightening
     ------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    /* Title can scale down a touch on tightest screens */
    .ds-pdp__info-title { font-size: clamp(30px, 9vw, 48px); }

    /* Price shrinks slightly so it doesn't dwarf everything */
    .ds-pdp__info-price { font-size: 24px; }
    .ds-pdp__info-price-strike { font-size: 16px; }

    /* Tagline tightens its line length on narrow */
    .ds-pdp__info-tagline { font-size: 16px; max-width: none; }

    /* Gallery thumbs — keep 4 across, just tighten the gap so squares
       breathe more on narrow screens */
    .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs { gap: var(--space-2); }

    /* Specs — long values were colliding with labels in the flex layout.
       Stack label above value with a small gap on mobile. */
    .ds-pdp__info-spec {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 4px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
    }
    .ds-pdp__info-spec-value { text-align: left; }
  }

  /* ============================================================
     STICKY ADD-TO-CART BAR
     Fixed at top, slides down once the main ATC scrolls out of view.
     Sits below the sticky header so the header nav stays accessible.
     ============================================================ */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta {
    position: fixed;
    /* --ds-search-top tracks the live bottom edge of the header (set by
       JS in ds-header.liquid). This accounts for the announce bar +
       sticky header state. Falls back to header height. */
    top: var(--ds-search-top, var(--header-height, 64px));
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 45;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-fg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    transform: translateY(-110%);
    transition:
      transform  var(--t-base, 240ms) var(--ease, cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)),
      visibility var(--t-base, 240ms) var(--ease, cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1));
    visibility: hidden;
    /* Reset inherited form layout */
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta.is-visible {
    transform: translateY(0);
    visibility: visible;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--pad-x);
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    min-height: 64px;
  }

  /* Thumbnail — click to scroll back to top */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media {
    display: block;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Name + price */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__info {
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-feature-settings: "tnum";
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price-strike {
    text-decoration: line-through;
    color: var(--color-fg-faint);
    margin-right: 6px;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* ATC button — mono caps brutalist */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn {
    background: var(--color-fg);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: background var(--t-fast) var(--ease), color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent-fg);
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-icon {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  /* Show short "Add" on phones, full "Add to cart" on bigger screens */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label { display: inline; }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 500px) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label { display: none; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long { display: inline; }
  }

  /* Mobile — tighter padding, smaller thumb */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      min-height: 56px;
    }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name { font-size: 13px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price { font-size: 12px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn { padding: 10px 14px; }
  }

  /* Reduced motion: drop the slide, just toggle visibility */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta { transition: none; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Disrupted PDP main",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ds-section ds-section--pdp-main",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1",
      "label": "Color scheme"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Sub-CTA below buy button"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sub_cta_label",
      "label": "Label",
      "default": "Watch the demo",
      "info": "Text on the secondary link below the Add-to-cart button. Leave blank to hide entirely."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sub_cta_url",
      "label": "Link or anchor",
      "default": "#video",
      "info": "Use an in-page anchor (#video, #specimen, #features, #includes) to smooth-scroll to that section, OR a full https:// URL for an external link. Hardcoded per template — each product type's template ships with the right defaults."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Gallery behavior" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "auto_advance_to_second",
      "label": "Auto-advance to 2nd media on load",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Keeps the cover image as media position 1 (so it stays the collection-grid thumbnail), but the PDP main view swaps to media position 2 on load. Useful for plugin templates where you want the demo video to play immediately while still using a static thumbnail elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gallery_pagination_style",
      "label": "Pagination style",
      "options": [
        { "value": "thumbnails", "label": "Thumbnail grid (4-column)" },
        { "value": "dots", "label": "Dot pagination (editorial)" }
      ],
      "default": "thumbnails",
      "info": "Thumbnails show every media as a small preview; better for fonts / graphics where each item sells differently. Dots are minimal pills below the main; better for plugins where one demo video does the selling. Both modes always show the X / N counter overlay in the bottom-right of the main."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Description" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "description_clamp_lines",
      "label": "Read more — clamp to N lines",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
      "info": "Description clips after this many lines and shows a 'Read more' toggle. Set higher (8-12) for templates where you want most of the description visible by default. The toggle auto-hides if the description is short enough not to need clipping."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Disrupted PDP main"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

<script>
  // Gallery — thumbnail swap + inset prev/next arrow nav
  //
  // Scopes everything to the nearest `.ds-pdp__gallery` so multiple
  // galleries on a page (shouldn't happen on PDP but safe) don't
  // collide.  The `activate(btn)` helper is the single source of
  // truth: thumbnail click and arrow click both funnel through it,
  // so the active state + main-image swap stay consistent.
  //
  // Arrows wrap at ends (prev from index 0 jumps to the last image,
  // next from the last image jumps back to 0).
  (function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('.ds-pdp__gallery').forEach(function (gallery) {
      var mainSlot = gallery.querySelector('.ds-pdp__gallery-main');
      var thumbs   = gallery.querySelector('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs');
      if (!mainSlot || !thumbs) return;

      var thumbList = Array.prototype.slice.call(
        thumbs.querySelectorAll('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumb'));

      // Current main element (img or video) — re-queried each activate so
      // we can swap between element types.
      function getCurrentMain() {
        return mainSlot.querySelector('.ds-pdp__gallery-main-img, .ds-pdp__gallery-main-video');
      }

      // Cache the counter element once — referenced on every activate()
      // to keep the "X / N" overlay in sync with the visible media.
      var counterCurrentEl = gallery.querySelector('[data-counter-current]');

      function activate(btn) {
        if (!btn) return;
        thumbList.forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-active'); });
        btn.classList.add('is-active');

        // Update the counter pill, if it's rendered (only when media > 1).
        if (counterCurrentEl) {
          var idx = thumbList.indexOf(btn);
          if (idx >= 0) counterCurrentEl.textContent = (idx + 1);
        }

        var mediaType = btn.getAttribute('data-media-type') || 'image';
        var current = getCurrentMain();

        // If the currently-displayed main is a video, run its cleanup
        // handler before replacing it. The cleanup detaches the
        // visibility-change listener that the previous video attached
        // to document — without this, every video-thumbnail click
        // leaks a listener that survives the video element being GC'd.
        if (current && current.tagName === 'VIDEO' && typeof current._dsCleanup === 'function') {
          current._dsCleanup();
        }

        if (mediaType === 'video') {
          // Build a fresh <video> element with autoplay/muted/loop/controls.
          // The current main (image or stale video) gets replaced wholesale.
          var vsrc = btn.getAttribute('data-video-src');
          if (!vsrc) return; // graceful no-op — Liquid didn't find an mp4 source

          var video = document.createElement('video');
          video.className = 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img ds-pdp__gallery-main-video';
          video.setAttribute('autoplay', '');
          video.setAttribute('muted', '');
          video.setAttribute('loop', '');
          video.setAttribute('playsinline', '');
          // Native controls intentionally omitted — gallery video is an
          // ambient autoplay loop, not a media player. Use the hero
          // pixel-perfect demo button if you want a click-to-play
          // experience with controls in a modal.
          video.setAttribute('preload', 'auto');
          // disableRemotePlayback prevents iOS AirPlay icon from appearing
          // and reduces edge-case autoplay rejections.
          video.setAttribute('disableRemotePlayback', '');
          video.muted = true; // explicit JS prop — required for autoplay in Chrome/Safari
          var poster = btn.getAttribute('data-video-poster');
          if (poster) video.poster = poster;
          video.src = vsrc;

          if (current) {
            current.replaceWith(video);
          } else {
            mainSlot.insertBefore(video, mainSlot.firstChild);
          }

          // Robust autoplay with retries.
          //
          // The intermittent mobile-autoplay-failure case: video element
          // is created + inserted, then play() is called synchronously
          // — but the video has no data yet. The play() promise rejects
          // silently (commonly NotAllowedError on iOS, AbortError on
          // Chrome), and no further play() is ever attempted, so the
          // video sits frozen on its poster until the user taps it.
          //
          // Fix: retry play() at three escalating readiness moments —
          // 'loadedmetadata' (we know the duration/dimensions), 'canplay'
          // (we have enough data to start), and 'canplaythrough' (we
          // can play start-to-finish without buffering). Any of them
          // succeeding kicks autoplay on. attemptPlay short-circuits if
          // the video is already playing so the retries are no-ops.
          function attemptPlay() {
            if (!video.paused) return; // already running
            var p = video.play();
            if (p && p.catch) {
              p.catch(function (err) {
                console.warn('[ds-pdp-gallery] video.play() rejected:', err.name, err.message);
              });
            }
          }
          video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', attemptPlay);
          video.addEventListener('canplay', attemptPlay);
          video.addEventListener('canplaythrough', attemptPlay);
          // Also retry when the page becomes visible again — covers the
          // case where the user backgrounded the tab during initial load
          // and play() got rejected because the tab wasn't focused.
          var onVisibilityChange = function () {
            if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') attemptPlay();
          };
          document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', onVisibilityChange);
          // Clean up the visibility listener if this video element is
          // ever replaced (e.g. user clicks a different thumbnail).
          // We use a custom property because there's no clean
          // "video removed" event.
          video._dsCleanup = function () {
            document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', onVisibilityChange);
          };

          attemptPlay();
        } else {
          var src = btn.getAttribute('data-src');
          if (!src) return;

          if (current && current.tagName === 'IMG') {
            // Same element, just swap src. Wipe srcset so our src wins.
            current.removeAttribute('srcset');
            current.removeAttribute('sizes');
            current.src = src;
          } else {
            // Replacing a video with an image — build a new <img>.
            var img = document.createElement('img');
            img.className = 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img';
            img.src = src;
            img.alt = '';
            if (current) {
              current.replaceWith(img);
            } else {
              mainSlot.insertBefore(img, mainSlot.firstChild);
            }
          }
        }
      }

      // Thumbnail click — direct activation.
      thumbs.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var btn = e.target.closest('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumb');
        if (!btn) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        activate(btn);
      });

      // Inset arrow nav — step ±1 through thumbList, wrap at ends.
      function step(delta) {
        if (thumbList.length === 0) return;
        var currentIdx = thumbList.findIndex(function (b) {
          return b.classList.contains('is-active');
        });
        if (currentIdx === -1) currentIdx = 0;
        var nextIdx = (currentIdx + delta + thumbList.length) % thumbList.length;
        activate(thumbList[nextIdx]);
      }
      var prevBtn = gallery.querySelector('[data-ds-gallery-prev]');
      var nextBtn = gallery.querySelector('[data-ds-gallery-next]');
      if (prevBtn) {
        prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          step(-1);
        });
      }
      if (nextBtn) {
        nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          step(1);
        });
      }

      // ----- Mobile swipe — touch left/right on the main media area
      // cycles to the prev/next thumbnail. ~50px horizontal threshold
      // filters accidental taps. Vertical drags (dy > dx) cancel the
      // gesture so the page can still scroll naturally if a finger
      // happens to land on the gallery while scrolling.
      //
      // All listeners are passive — we never preventDefault, so iOS
      // doesn't downgrade scroll performance. Mouse devices don't fire
      // touch events, so desktop UX is unaffected (arrows + thumb
      // click stay as the only desktop affordance).
      var touchStartX = 0;
      var touchStartY = 0;
      var isTracking = false;
      var SWIPE_PX = 50;

      mainSlot.addEventListener('touchstart', function (e) {
        if (e.touches.length !== 1) return;
        touchStartX = e.touches[0].clientX;
        touchStartY = e.touches[0].clientY;
        isTracking = true;
      }, { passive: true });

      mainSlot.addEventListener('touchmove', function (e) {
        if (!isTracking) return;
        var dx = e.touches[0].clientX - touchStartX;
        var dy = e.touches[0].clientY - touchStartY;
        // If the gesture is dominantly vertical, abandon swipe-tracking
        // so the user can scroll the page through the gallery.
        if (Math.abs(dy) > Math.abs(dx)) {
          isTracking = false;
        }
      }, { passive: true });

      mainSlot.addEventListener('touchend', function (e) {
        if (!isTracking) return;
        isTracking = false;
        var dx = e.changedTouches[0].clientX - touchStartX;
        if (Math.abs(dx) < SWIPE_PX) return;
        // Swipe right (positive dx) → previous; swipe left → next
        step(dx > 0 ? -1 : 1);
      }, { passive: true });

      // ----- Auto-advance to the 2nd media on load -----
      // Some product templates (e.g. plugins) want the demo video to
      // be the default main view instead of the featured/cover image
      // — but we still want the cover image to be the FIRST media so
      // it stays the thumbnail on collection grids. So: keep the
      // featured image at position 0, and have JS swap the main view
      // to position 1 (the video) immediately on page load. The user
      // toggles this per-section via the 'auto_advance_to_second'
      // setting on ds-product-main; only renders the data attribute
      // when both enabled AND there are 2+ media items.
      if (gallery.getAttribute('data-auto-advance') === '1' && thumbList.length > 1) {
        activate(thumbList[1]);
      }

      // Eager-preload every non-active thumb's full-size image into the
      // browser cache so switching between gallery images is instant
      // instead of triggering a fresh network request on every click.
      //
      // Why this matters: the activate() function above just sets
      // mainImg.src = data-src. Without preload, the browser fetches
      // that URL on the click, which is what was causing the lag on
      // the first switch (only fast on repeat clicks because of cache).
      //
      // Timing: deferred to requestIdleCallback (or setTimeout fallback
      // for older Safari) so we don't compete with the main image's
      // fetchpriority=high load, which has to finish first for LCP.
      // By the time the user clicks a thumb (usually multiple seconds
      // in), the preload has completed and the swap hits cache.
      //
      // Priority: low fetchPriority hint so these loads stay polite —
      // they shouldn't slow down anything above-the-fold.
      function preloadGalleryImages() {
        // Skip first thumb — its URL matches the main image's src so
        // the high-res version is already in cache.
        thumbList.slice(1).forEach(function (btn) {
          var src = btn.getAttribute('data-src');
          if (!src) return;
          var img = new Image();
          if ('fetchPriority' in img) img.fetchPriority = 'low';
          img.src = src;
        });
      }
      if ('requestIdleCallback' in window) {
        requestIdleCallback(preloadGalleryImages, { timeout: 2000 });
      } else {
        setTimeout(preloadGalleryImages, 500);
      }
    });
  })();

  // ----- Aggregate star rating under the product title -----
  // Auto-populates the [data-ds-rating] placeholder by scanning the
  // page for testimonials flagged as linked to this product (cards
  // with .ds-testimonials__item--current — added by the Liquid in
  // ds-testimonials.liquid). For each matching card, reads its
  // [aria-label="Rated N out of 5"] to get the rating, averages
  // across all cards, and renders stars + review count.
  //
  // If no matching cards are on the page, the placeholder stays
  // [hidden] and nothing renders. Same for the no-JS / blocked-JS
  // fallback case — the buy box reads exactly as it did before.
  (function () {
    function init() {
      var display = document.querySelector('[data-ds-rating]');
      if (!display) return;

      var cards = document.querySelectorAll('.ds-testimonials__item--current');
      if (cards.length === 0) return;

      var total = 0;
      var counted = 0;
      cards.forEach(function (card) {
        var ratingEl = card.querySelector('.ds-testimonials__rating');
        if (!ratingEl) return;
        var label = ratingEl.getAttribute('aria-label') || '';
        var match = label.match(/(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\s*out\s*of/i);
        if (!match) return;
        total += parseFloat(match[1]);
        counted++;
      });

      if (counted === 0) return;

      var avg = total / counted;
      var rounded = Math.round(avg);
      var stars = '';
      for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) stars += i < rounded ? '★' : '☆';

      var starsEl = display.querySelector('[data-ds-rating-stars]');
      var textEl = display.querySelector('[data-ds-rating-text]');
      if (starsEl) starsEl.textContent = stars;
      if (textEl) {
        textEl.textContent = '(' + counted + ' review' + (counted === 1 ? '' : 's') + ')';
      }
      display.hidden = false;
    }

    // Run after DOMContentLoaded so the testimonials section markup
    // is in place (it's lower in the document order).
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }
  })();

  // ----- Description "Read more" toggle -----
  // Auto-hides itself when the description fits inside the clamp
  // (short descriptions don't need a toggle). Reads the clamp line
  // count from data-clamp-lines on the wrapper so it can be tuned
  // per-section via the description_clamp_lines setting without
  // touching CSS.
  (function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-ds-desc]').forEach(function (wrap) {
      var body = wrap.querySelector('[data-ds-desc-body]');
      var toggle = wrap.querySelector('[data-ds-desc-toggle]');
      if (!body || !toggle) return;

      // Apply the clamp value from data-* to a CSS var the body reads.
      var clampLines = parseInt(wrap.getAttribute('data-clamp-lines'), 10) || 4;
      body.style.setProperty('--ds-desc-clamp', clampLines);

      var labelMore = toggle.querySelector('[data-ds-desc-toggle-label-more]');
      var labelLess = toggle.querySelector('[data-ds-desc-toggle-label-less]');

      function refreshOverflowState() {
        // Temporarily un-clamp to measure the unclipped scroll height.
        var wasClamped = !wrap.classList.contains('is-expanded');
        if (wasClamped) {
          // Compare full content height (scrollHeight) to the clipped
          // height (clientHeight). If they match, no overflow — hide
          // the toggle entirely. Add a 2px fudge factor for sub-pixel
          // rounding differences across browsers.
          var overflows = body.scrollHeight > body.clientHeight + 2;
          toggle.hidden = !overflows;
        }
      }

      // Initial measurement after layout / fonts settle. Fonts can
      // re-layout text after first paint and change overflow state,
      // so check once on DOMContentLoaded and once after fonts load.
      refreshOverflowState();
      if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) {
        document.fonts.ready.then(refreshOverflowState);
      }
      // Recheck on resize because viewport width changes wrap-points
      // and can flip overflow state.
      var resizeTimer;
      window.addEventListener('resize', function () {
        clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
        resizeTimer = setTimeout(refreshOverflowState, 150);
      }, { passive: true });

      toggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var nowExpanded = !wrap.classList.contains('is-expanded');
        wrap.classList.toggle('is-expanded', nowExpanded);
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', nowExpanded ? 'true' : 'false');
        if (labelMore) labelMore.hidden = nowExpanded;
        if (labelLess) labelLess.hidden = !nowExpanded;
      });
    });
  })();

  // Sub-CTA smooth-scroll — if the demo_url metafield is a #anchor
  // (e.g. "#video", "#features"), intercept the click and smooth-scroll
  // to that PDP section, offset by the sticky header height. Full URLs
  // (https://…, /pages/…) fall through to normal navigation.
  (function () {
    var link = document.querySelector('.ds-pdp__info-sub-cta a');
    if (!link) return;
    var href = link.getAttribute('href') || '';
    if (href.charAt(0) !== '#' || href.length < 2) return;

    link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var target = document.querySelector(href);
      if (!target) return;
      e.preventDefault();

      // For the type specimen specifically, auto-open the glyph dropdown
      // before scrolling. Otherwise clicking "VIEW FULL SPECIMEN" lands
      // the user on a collapsed accordion and they'd have to click again.
      // FAQ details intentionally stay closed (different UX expectation).
      target.querySelectorAll('details.ds-pdp-typespecimen__details:not([open])').forEach(function (d) {
        d.open = true;
      });

      var header = document.querySelector('.ds-header');
      var offset = (header ? header.offsetHeight : 64) + 16;
      var y = target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - offset;
      window.scrollTo({ top: y, behavior: 'smooth' });
    });
  })();

  // Sticky ATC bar — show when the main ATC has scrolled above the
  // header, hide when it's back in view. Also sync variant + price
  // between the main form and the sticky form so the right variant
  // is added when the user has picked one.
  (function () {
    var bar       = document.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-cta]');
    var mainAtc   = document.querySelector('[data-ds-main-atc]');
    if (!bar || !mainAtc) return;

    function getHeaderBottom() {
      // Prefer live measurement (announce bar may be in view, or not)
      var hdr = document.querySelector('.ds-header');
      if (hdr) {
        var b = hdr.getBoundingClientRect().bottom;
        if (b > 0) return b;
      }
      // Fallback: read --ds-search-top (updated live by ds-header JS)
      var v = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--ds-search-top');
      var n = parseInt(v, 10);
      if (n > 0) return n;
      // Last resort
      return 64;
    }

    var ticking = false;
    function update() {
      var rect = mainAtc.getBoundingClientRect();
      var threshold = getHeaderBottom();
      // Show once the main ATC's bottom edge has scrolled above the
      // bottom of the sticky header (with a small buffer).
      var shouldShow = rect.bottom < threshold + 4;
      bar.classList.toggle('is-visible', shouldShow);
      bar.setAttribute('aria-hidden', shouldShow ? 'false' : 'true');
      ticking = false;
    }
    function onScrollOrResize() {
      if (!ticking) {
        requestAnimationFrame(update);
        ticking = true;
      }
    }

    update();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScrollOrResize, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', onScrollOrResize, { passive: true });

    // Click the sticky thumbnail → scroll back to top of the PDP
    var topLink = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-top]');
    if (topLink) {
      topLink.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    }

    // Sync variant + price between the main form and the sticky form.
    // Handles both control types — <select> for normal variants, and the
    // tier-cards radio group when the product has license-tier metafields.
    var mainSelect    = document.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-select]');
    var mainRadios    = document.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-radio-group]');
    var stickyVariant = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-variant]');
    var stickyPrice   = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-price]');
    var stickyCompare = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-compare]');

    function applyToSticky(control) {
      if (!control) return;
      var newValue         = control.getAttribute('value') || control.value;
      var priceCents       = parseInt(control.getAttribute('data-price'), 10);
      var compareCents     = parseInt(control.getAttribute('data-compare-at'), 10) || 0;
      var priceFormatted   = control.getAttribute('data-price-formatted') || '';
      var compareFormatted = control.getAttribute('data-compare-formatted') || '';

      if (stickyVariant) stickyVariant.value = newValue;
      if (stickyPrice && priceFormatted) stickyPrice.textContent = priceFormatted;

      // Strike-through compare — show only when the variant is
      // actually on sale (compare > price > 0). Previously the
      // sticky bar's whole .price element was overwritten on each
      // change, which clobbered the strike; now strike + price are
      // separate spans we toggle independently.
      if (stickyCompare) {
        var onSale = compareCents > priceCents && compareCents > 0;
        if (onSale) {
          stickyCompare.textContent = compareFormatted;
          stickyCompare.removeAttribute('hidden');
        } else {
          stickyCompare.setAttribute('hidden', '');
        }
      }
    }

    if (mainSelect && stickyVariant) {
      mainSelect.addEventListener('change', function () {
        applyToSticky(mainSelect.options[mainSelect.selectedIndex]);
      });
    }

    if (mainRadios && stickyVariant) {
      mainRadios.addEventListener('change', function (e) {
        if (!e.target || !e.target.matches('input[type="radio"]')) return;
        applyToSticky(e.target);
      });
    }
  })();
</script>
